{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100463","id":2236955413,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6FVTsV","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100463","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100463.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100463.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100463","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100463/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100463/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100463/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fe3aaa2ae3804ac25a76495c6262dbce07211a66","number":100463,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add ability to apply forces and impulses to `SoftBody3D`","user":{"login":"PiCode9560","id":122909224,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1NyKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122909224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560","html_url":"https://github.com/PiCode9560","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1013\r\n\r\nThe goal of this PR is to add `apply_impulse` and `apply_force` to the `Softbody` node\r\n\r\nAdding them to the `GodotPhysics` and `JoltPhysics`.\r\n\r\n# Added functions\r\n**Softbody3D:**\r\n`void apply_central_force(force: Vector3)`\r\n`void apply_force(force: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n`void apply_central_impulse(impulse: Vector3)`\r\n`void apply_impulse(impulse: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n\r\n**PhysicsServer3D:**\r\n`void soft_body_apply_central_force(body: RID, force: Vector3)`\r\n`void soft_body_apply_central_impulse(body: RID, impulse: Vector3)`\r\n`void soft_body_apply_point_force(body: RID, force: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n`void soft_body_apply_point_impulse(body: RID, impulse: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n\r\n# Built-in documentation\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: I think these are a bit outdated\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Show documentation</summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n## PhysicsServer3D\r\n\r\n>`● void soft_body_apply_central_force(body: RID, force: Vector3)`\r\n> \r\n>Distributes and applies an force to all vertices. A force is time dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void soft_body_apply_central_impulse(body: RID, impulse: Vector3)`\r\n> \r\n> Distributes and applies an impulse to all vertices.\r\n> \r\n> An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void soft_body_apply_point_force(body: RID, force: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n> \r\n> Applies a force to a vertex. A force is time dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void soft_body_apply_point_impulse(body: RID, impulse: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n> \r\n> Applies an impulse to a vertex.\r\n> \r\n> An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\r\n\r\n## SoftBody3D\r\n\r\n> `● void apply_central_force(force: Vector3)`\r\n>\r\n> Distributes and applies an force to all vertices. A force is time dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void apply_central_impulse(impulse: Vector3)`\r\n>\r\n> Distributes and applies an impulse to all vertices.\r\n> \r\n> An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void apply_force(force: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n> \r\n> Applies a force to a vertex. A force is time dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\r\n\r\n\r\n> `● void apply_impulse(impulse: Vector3, point_index: int)`\r\n> \r\n> Applies an impulse to a vertex.\r\n> \r\n> An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Demo\r\n\r\nDemo project: [godot-softbody-apply-force-and-impulse-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19620871/godot-softbody-apply-force-and-impulse-test.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\nThese are how the functions compared to rigidbody.\r\n\r\nThe impulses have a strength of 0.2.\r\nThe forces have a strength of 15.\r\n\r\n### Jolt physics:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a781599-1a6d-4ba4-804c-c3b230b152ba\r\n\r\n### Godot physics:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/025d1047-9319-4db6-9bb7-7865b0f5d91c\r\n\r\n### Player Controller (Jolt physics):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/84ba9d9c-8dd7-49d9-a557-4115a61be1cd\r\n\r\n# Implementation Details\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Godot apply_impulse</summary>\r\n\r\n`GodotSoftbody3D` already have `apply_node_impulse` method which apply impulse to a vertex. So I just use that for the `softbody.apply_impulse`.\r\n</details>\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Godot apply_force</summary>\r\n\r\n`GodotSoftbody3D` have `vertex.f` which stores the applied forces, and it will handle it somewhere. Therefore, I only need to add a method that add the forces to it.\r\n</details>\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Jolt apply_impulse</summary>\r\n\r\n`JoltSoftbody3D` didn't have a method to apply impulse. So I added  `JoltSoftBody3D::apply_node_impulse`. It works like the `GodotSoftBody3D::apply_node_impulse` which just add `impulse * vertex.inverse_mass` to the vertex velocity.\r\n</details>\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Jolt apply_force</summary>\r\n\r\n[Outdated]\r\nI notice that the core JoltPhysics didn't have a way to apply force to softbody vertex. Hence, I have to add that functionality into the core of the JoltPhysics engine.\r\n\r\nI added `vertex.mForce`, which store the forces that are going to be applied. Then applies it in the `SoftBodyMotionProperties::IntegratePositions` and reset the force on `SoftBodyMotionProperties::UpdateSoftBodyState`.\r\n</details>\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>apply_central_impulse/force</summary>\r\n\r\nFor `SoftBody.apply_central_impulse` and `SoftBody.apply_central_force` I added `apply_central_impulse` and `apply_central_force` methods to jolt and godot. It works like the `apply_node_impulse/force` but the impulse/force is divided by the vertex count and applies it to all vertices.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z"},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-12-16T10:19:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T12:37:31Z","closed_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:23Z","merged_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:23Z","merge_commit_sha":"de2cd663fdf9d824eba99d101b56011b346175c7","a